---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import InformationNav from '../../components/InformationNav.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const levels = [
  ['Strong', 'Independently reproduced or supported by multiple strong sources.'],
  [
    'Primary',
    'A first-party paper, repository, release note, lab, or vendor source. A primary source can still make an unverified claim.',
  ],
  ['Preliminary', 'Early research or a preprint without strong independent validation.'],
  ['Anecdotal', 'A practitioner report or limited case study that may not generalize.'],
  ['Unverified', 'A notable claim without enough support to treat it as established.'],
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Editorial methodology — The Daily AI Pulse"
  description="How Pulse selects stories, labels evidence, and handles corrections."
>
  <article class="information-page">
    <p class="eyebrow">EDITORIAL STANDARD</p>
    <h1>How we choose the signal.</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      The question behind each story: what changed, how do we know, and what should an engineer do
      with it?
    </p>
    <div class="information-grid">
      <InformationNav active="methodology" />
      <div class="information-content">
        <section>
          <h2>Selection</h2>
          <p>
            We prioritize significance, evidence, novelty, relevance to engineering, and lasting
            usefulness. The score informs a human editorial choice. We prefer a short issue to a
            padded one, and avoid repeating a recent story unless there is a meaningful new
            development.
          </p>
          <p>
            We favor original papers, technical reports, specifications, repositories, release
            notes, and incident reports. Vendor claims are attributed to their source; a benchmark
            headline is examined for what it actually measures.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h2>Evidence labels</h2>
          <dl class="evidence-list">
            {levels.map(([term, definition]) => (
              <div>
                <dt>{term}</dt>
                <dd>{definition}</dd>
              </div>
            ))}
          </dl>
          <p>
            Evidence describes support for a claim. Signal describes editorial importance. A
            high-signal story can still have preliminary evidence, and those ideas should not be
            confused.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h2>Reporting and corrections</h2>
          <p>
            Stories link their sources and separate factual reporting from editorial interpretation,
            including a labeled Pulse Take where useful. Research coverage should identify preprints
            and meaningful limits.
          </p>
          <p>
            If something is wrong,{' '}
            <a href="https://github.com/GadDev/daily-ai-pulse/issues/new/choose">
              request a correction
            </a>{' '}
            with a source and the affected story. Corrections are recorded on the story when
            published. For more detail, read the{' '}
            <a href="https://github.com/GadDev/daily-ai-pulse/blob/main/docs/EDITORIAL.md">
              full editorial guide
            </a>
            .
          </p>
        </section>
        <p class="return-link">
          <a href={`${base}about/`}>← About Pulse</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .evidence-list {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .evidence-list div {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 9rem 1fr;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    padding: 0.9rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  dt {
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  dd {
    margin: 0;
  }
  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .evidence-list div {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 0.2rem;
    }
  }
</style>
